=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# Warning$
# Before disabling root SSH login, ensure:$
$
   -  Non-root user has sudo privileges$
   -  Non-root user SSH access has been tested$
   -  If SSH fails, a fallback access method is available$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Root SSH Login       Enabled$
   -  SSH Port             2230$
   -  Allowed Users        alice$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Set PermitRootLogin no$
$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
      @@ -1,3 +1,3 @@$
       # Managed by hardn$
       Port 2230$
      -PermitRootLogin yes$
      +PermitRootLogin no$
      $ sshd -t$
      $ systemctl reload ssh$
$
  Disable SSH login for 'root'?$
$
  Type the hostname [bos-san-l01, 0 or q]: y$
  [!] Error: That does not match exactly. Please try again.$
  Type the hostname [bos-san-l01, 0 or q]: bos-san-l01$
$
  [+] Done: Set PermitRootLogin no$
$
# Operation Successful$

